--- !u!114 &1473024705
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1473024703}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 871a59ef81fc4408f9f098fcacfc07ab, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Stereopsis.Readable
  title: Carbon copy - The Harbour Echo, November 1922
  body: 'THREE INCHES ON PAGE ELEVEN.


    A servant hanged in 1699 may have been
    innocent of murder. The evidence, assembled by a woman of the household in 1861
    and verified where verification is possible, points instead to the merchant Elias
    Vane.


    They set it between a furniture advertisement and the tide tables.


    No
    one wrote. No one called at the office. A man is two centuries dead and I could
    not make one reader care for him.


    [placeholder text - the real page eleven
    is Simon''s to write]'
  setsFlag: 
